  "comment": "Parameters 18, 19 and 20 (mutate, randomise and clear) are configured but no widget is added for any of them, so no click can reach them; parameters 62 to 77 (expression curve and power) are driven by an XY pad added with addParam and no paramId, which the census records as index -1, so they cannot be tagged either. Both groups are covered by Note lines instead.\nThe panel prints SHIFT and LEN twice each in the lower left block, once over a knob and once over the jack beneath it, and SHIFT a third time over the pattern-shift knob in the middle; the lines say which is which rather than repeating the word.\nThe two expression outputs are marked only by glyphs — a curve over the first and a plus over the second — with the word EXPR between them. The maker's own tooltips name them Expression and Expression Curve, and that is the order the widget adds them in (PhasequeWidget.cpp:207-209).\nIn Polyphonic and Muta-Unison modes the LEN output carries the step shift rather than the step length: Phaseque.cpp:663 reads StepAttr::STEP_SHIFT where the monophonic path at Phaseque.cpp:614 reads STEP_LEN, and the polyphonic line also omits the * 5.f the monophonic one applies. That looks like a copy-and-paste fault in the maker's source; the LEN output's line describes the monophonic behaviour, which is the default."
